WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.209 --> 00:00:04.170 line:68%
Every year through
the annual budget process

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.756 line:68%
Yale thoroughly reviews
its financial resources

00:00:06.756 --> 00:00:07.841 line:71%
and the strategic goals

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:10.093 line:68%
that serve to advance
the university's mission.

00:00:10.927 --> 00:00:14.389 line:68%
We carefully consider new
and continuing opportunities

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:16.808
for supporting students, faculty
and staff

00:00:17.225 --> 00:00:18.935
across the university

00:00:18.935 --> 00:00:21.396
and for partnering with our home
city of New Haven.

00:00:22.272 --> 00:00:25.692
The purpose of this video
is to explain where funding for

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:28.319
the budget comes from,
how it's allocated,

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:32.282
and how we make those decisions.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:37.370
[upbeat music]

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:41.583
(Scott)
The university budget falls
into two basic categories.

00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:45.628
First is the operating budget,
which is the ongoing costs

00:00:45.628 --> 00:00:47.756
of what it takes
to run a university

00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:49.799
on a day to day basis
throughout the year.

00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:52.802
The other is the capital budget
and the capital budget

00:00:52.802 --> 00:00:55.597
is what it takes to be able
to build new buildings

00:00:55.597 --> 00:00:58.558
or renovate existing buildings
for their use.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:00:59.851 align:start position:0% line:71%
One key to the budget

00:00:59.851 --> 00:01:02.395 align:start position:0% line:68%
is that this is incredibly
collaborative.

00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:03.855 align:start position:0% line:71%
It involves input from

00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:05.899 align:start position:0% line:68%
so many different places
in the university,

00:01:06.191 --> 00:01:08.067 line:71%
all of whom are working together

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:11.404
to try to develop a budget
by late spring

00:01:11.696 --> 00:01:13.573
that can be approved
by the corporation

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:16.326
and then move forward to define
spending in the coming year.

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:19.245
This begins
with a set of parameters

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.915
that are given
to each budgetary unit

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:25.376
that define things like what
we anticipate inflation

00:01:25.376 --> 00:01:28.880
will be, what we anticipate
the endowment return will be.

00:01:29.172 --> 00:01:30.924
Those are then brought back
to what's called

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.801
the Budget Advisory Group.

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:36.012
The Budget Advisory Group
is comprised of the provost,

00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:39.766
those in the Provost Office,
senior administrative leadership

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:42.560
in the Department
of Finance and Operations,

00:01:42.852 --> 00:01:45.980
as well as several faculty
that provide perspective

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:49.025
and input to understand
both the financial side

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:52.779
as well as the academic side
of all these budget requests.

00:01:52.987 --> 00:01:55.156
We work to create a budget
which reflects

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:59.244
our current needs,
but also reflects the need to be

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:02.539
financially responsible
into future generations.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:03.790
External revenue

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.668
for the operating budget
comes from a variety of sources.

00:02:06.876 --> 00:02:11.297
For the past year, 2022,
which runs from July 1st 2021

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.508
until June 30th 2022.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.346
That revenue contributes just
over $4.7 billion to the budget.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.559 align:end position:100% line:0%
It might be surprising to
see that tuition, room and board

00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:25.770 line:0%
comprise a relatively small
slice of this overall revenue.

00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:30.859 line:0%
It's just $450 million or about
10% of the university budget.

00:02:31.776 --> 00:02:35.530 align:end position:100% line:0%
That's the net amount
after 50% of the gross tuition

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:38.157 align:end position:100% line:0%
room and board is returned
in the form of financial aid.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.326 align:end position:100% line:0%
The two biggest
sources of income

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:43.538 align:end position:100% line:0%
are spending from the endowment,
which contributes about

00:02:43.538 --> 00:02:46.207 align:start size:56% position:44% line:0%
1.6 billion or 33%

00:02:46.207 --> 00:02:47.834 size:88% position:56% line:0%
and medical services income,

00:02:48.209 --> 00:02:52.088 align:end position:100% line:0%
which is 1.4 billion
or 29% of the total budget.

00:02:53.089 --> 00:02:55.675 align:end position:100% line:0%
The third largest
contributor of revenue is grants

00:02:55.675 --> 00:03:00.597 align:end position:100% line:0%
and contracts
at $921 million or 19%

00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:02.348 align:start size:63% position:38% line:0%
of the total budget.

00:03:02.807 --> 00:03:05.768
[thoughtful music]

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:09.397 line:78%
Yale's annual operating budget

00:03:09.397 --> 00:03:12.525 line:76%
is a combination
of all the sources of revenue

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.402 line:76%
we anticipate
for the coming year

00:03:14.402 --> 00:03:18.072 line:76%
as well as all of the expenses
or spending we anticipate

00:03:18.072 --> 00:03:19.240 line:78%
for the coming year.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.869
Every year the anticipated
expenses of the annual budget

00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:26.164
are typically close to the
amount of anticipated revenue.

00:03:27.165 --> 00:03:31.127
For the fiscal year 2022,
expected expenses

00:03:31.127 --> 00:03:34.964
net of internal revenue
are about $4.6 billion.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:39.218
Yale seeks to improve the world
by creating knowledge

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:40.678
and sharing that knowledge,

00:03:40.678 --> 00:03:43.723
and that's a mission that's
carried out by and for people.

00:03:44.432 --> 00:03:47.018
So it makes sense
that the biggest category

00:03:47.018 --> 00:03:48.937
of expenses at Yale

00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:51.522
are the salaries and benefits
for the people who work here.

00:03:51.522 --> 00:03:55.652
The nearly 5000 faculty
and about 10,000 staff.

00:03:55.985 --> 00:04:00.865 align:end position:100% line:53%
In the fiscal year 2022 budget,
salaries and benefits total

00:04:00.865 --> 00:04:02.700 align:end position:100% line:53%
$2.9 billion or
nearly two thirds

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.535 size:84% position:58% line:50%
of the university's budget.

00:04:05.703 --> 00:04:08.831 align:end position:100% line:53%
Included in the $2.9
billion is about

00:04:08.831 --> 00:04:11.626 align:end position:100% line:53%
$700 million in employee
benefit costs.

00:04:12.043 --> 00:04:15.880 align:end position:100% line:53%
Most of which over 90% are
health and retirement related.

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:20.176 align:end position:100%
Non-salary expenses account
for another $1.5 billion

00:04:20.176 --> 00:04:22.178 align:start size:44% position:56%
of the budget.

00:04:22.178 --> 00:04:25.598 align:end position:100%
These include a wide range
of costs, including utilities,

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:30.269
medical supplies and services,
lab supplies and equipment,

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:35.066 align:end position:100%
consulting and professional
services, acquisitions of books,

00:04:35.066 --> 00:04:38.528 align:end position:100%
periodicals and artworks,
and many other costs.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:41.114
You can find more details
on these expenses

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:43.408
and much more
about the operating budget

00:04:43.408 --> 00:04:44.951
in the University Budget book,

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.744 align:start position:0%
which is available
to all faculty,

00:04:46.744 --> 00:04:49.664 align:start position:0%
staff and students
on the Provost's website.

00:04:50.581 --> 00:04:54.335 line:76%
The Yale budget process
allows each school and unit to

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:57.338 line:76%
bring forward
their annual budget

00:04:57.338 --> 00:05:00.091 line:76%
in line with their strategic
initiatives that they've

00:05:00.091 --> 00:05:02.385 line:76%
put forth in a long range plan
for approval.

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:05.471
This is an opportunity for those
that get provostial funds

00:05:06.222 --> 00:05:08.766
to ask for funding for ideas
that they have

00:05:08.766 --> 00:05:11.769
put forward in line
with the mission of their school

00:05:11.769 --> 00:05:13.229
or in mission of the university.

00:05:13.229 --> 00:05:15.440
Once the officers, deans
and unit leaders,

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:16.816
along with their lead

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:19.360
administrators,
put together their proposals,

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.029
we meet with the Budget
Advisory Group

00:05:21.029 --> 00:05:23.031
during the months of March
and April.

00:05:23.197 --> 00:05:25.366
Everyone comes forward
and does a presentation.

00:05:25.366 --> 00:05:26.951
Decisions
are made really based on

00:05:26.951 --> 00:05:28.703
the operational
needs of the unit

00:05:28.703 --> 00:05:31.622
and we also look
at the president and provost

00:05:31.706 --> 00:05:34.208
strategic initiatives
for the next five to ten years.

00:05:34.417 --> 00:05:37.545
And we also look at
what ideas will

00:05:37.962 --> 00:05:39.547
have the strongest outcomes

00:05:39.547 --> 00:05:42.884
on the university and advance
the mission of the university.

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:46.804
We summarize the entire budget
for the provost

00:05:46.804 --> 00:05:48.639
who then presents it
to the president,

00:05:48.639 --> 00:05:50.767
who then presents it in
the June Corporation meeting

00:05:50.767 --> 00:05:53.978
to the trustees of Yale
University for approval.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:55.688
Once we gain approval,

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:57.607
we communicate
all that to the lead

00:05:57.607 --> 00:06:00.526
administrators, the deans
and officers for the new year,

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:01.694
and that happens in June

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:03.780
and we turn over the
new year July 1st.

00:06:04.238 --> 00:06:07.200
[inspiring music]

00:06:08.993 --> 00:06:10.828
Obviously the budget is

00:06:10.828 --> 00:06:12.580
everything
that is the university,

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:15.333
and so it supports everything
that is in the university:

00:06:15.333 --> 00:06:19.087
all the people, all the places,
all the collections,

00:06:19.295 --> 00:06:22.006
all the operations are supported
by this budget.

00:06:22.256 --> 00:06:25.551
It involves every aspect of what
the university does:

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.638
from the clinical practice
to what collections are found

00:06:28.638 --> 00:06:32.475
in the libraries, to what
the salaries are for faculty

00:06:32.475 --> 00:06:35.603
and staff, what financial aid
we provide to students.

00:06:36.187 --> 00:06:39.816
The most important thing
the university does is to

00:06:40.108 --> 00:06:42.360
recruit
the next generation of scholars

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.320
as we create
the community of scholars

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:46.030
that is Yale University.

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:49.325
The budget is the key tool
that we utilize for that

00:06:49.325 --> 00:06:52.245
recruitment as we further
diversify our faculty

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:56.666
and as we develop
the emerging fields

00:06:56.666 --> 00:06:59.585
that are happening across
different disciplines,

00:06:59.877 --> 00:07:01.629
it's a moment to reimagine

00:07:01.629 --> 00:07:03.464
what the fields are,
to reimagine

00:07:03.464 --> 00:07:04.924
what the university looks like,

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:07.176
what the composition
of the university is,

00:07:07.468 --> 00:07:10.304
and then to make these
investments in people

00:07:10.555 --> 00:07:11.639
and in the spaces

00:07:11.639 --> 00:07:14.016
that are needed for those people
to thrive.

00:07:14.016 --> 00:07:17.770
The generosity of our donors
over multiple decades

00:07:18.563 --> 00:07:22.441
makes it possible for us
to admit students without regard

00:07:22.441 --> 00:07:25.444
to their need, without regard
to their financial circumstance,

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.656
which is fundamentally
an opportunity

00:07:28.656 --> 00:07:30.616
to have the most diverse

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:33.995
student body possible
where we can recruit students

00:07:33.995 --> 00:07:37.123
to campus from all backgrounds
independent of what

00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:39.375
their financial resources
reflect

00:07:39.375 --> 00:07:41.961
that we can bring them
from really all over the world.

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:45.965
We can create the most diverse
student body utilizing the power

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:46.883
of the endowment

00:07:46.883 --> 00:07:49.760
to be able to cover the costs
of an education at Yale.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:52.263
The university's budget

00:07:52.263 --> 00:07:55.057
has to be part of building
an inclusive workplace.

00:07:55.349 --> 00:07:57.602
(Deborah)
When we start to think
about the composition

00:07:57.602 --> 00:07:59.061
of the organization,

00:07:59.061 --> 00:08:00.438
we think about faculty,

00:08:00.438 --> 00:08:01.814 line:71%
we think about students,

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:03.941 line:68%
we certainly think
about the 11,000

00:08:03.941 --> 00:08:06.194 line:68%
plus staff
that are part of the community.

00:08:06.194 --> 00:08:08.196 line:68%
But I also think the word
community is what's

00:08:08.196 --> 00:08:10.198 line:71%
most important to me.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:14.827
And so the university's budget
allows us to build community

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:16.579
through a variety
of different ways

00:08:16.579 --> 00:08:21.042
For staff diversity
it helps us to attract talent.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.045
The university's budget includes
a large commitment

00:08:24.045 --> 00:08:26.005
to the City of New Haven.

00:08:26.005 --> 00:08:30.176
I believe our commitment
is approximately $135 million

00:08:30.176 --> 00:08:32.011
over a six year period.

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:35.598
And as a result of that,
I think it makes us the largest

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:38.100
university
commitment to its host city.

00:08:38.601 --> 00:08:39.101
And for me

00:08:39.101 --> 00:08:41.646
that's quite exciting
given that I'm a resident and

00:08:41.646 --> 00:08:43.314
native of the city of New Haven.

00:08:43.314 --> 00:08:45.858
The budget process is dynamic.

00:08:45.858 --> 00:08:48.653
It reflects the revenue that's
coming into the university.

00:08:49.028 --> 00:08:50.613
Sometimes the endowment goes up

00:08:50.613 --> 00:08:53.032
and sometimes it goes down
and we have to make

00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:54.492
adjustments accordingly.

00:08:54.492 --> 00:08:58.204
And so through the generosity
of donors over

00:08:58.246 --> 00:09:00.414
multiple years, over centuries,

00:09:00.414 --> 00:09:02.124
that endowment
has grown to the point

00:09:02.124 --> 00:09:02.917
where it provides

00:09:02.917 --> 00:09:05.503
a substantial portion
of our budgetary support

00:09:06.087 --> 00:09:09.757
that makes it possible
for us to invest in the future,

00:09:09.924 --> 00:09:13.511
for us to carry out our mission,
for us to support our students

00:09:13.511 --> 00:09:15.179
and our faculty and our staff,

00:09:15.179 --> 00:09:16.889
to create
a community of scholars

00:09:16.889 --> 00:09:20.685
that is seeking the future
of academic disciplines

00:09:20.685 --> 00:09:22.728
and thriving
in all of its missions.

